{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310695,"nonce":"WXgNiKZIqaJLEga7d+5+QBMSf9k=","title":"FIXED in commit 38a9bb1. The compiler emits rayzor_pop_call_frame only before IrTerminator::Return, so every Throw whose longjmp bypasses ...","message":"**Status: FIXED** in commit `38a9bb1` (workflow `wbndzlgt6` Phase 2).\n\n\n`compiler/src/codegen/tiered_backend.rs:2049-2167` (`instrument_modules_for_stack_traces`) emits `rayzor_push_call_frame` at every function entry but `rayzor_pop_call_frame` only immediately before `IrTerminator::Return` blocks. Every Throw terminator's `_longjmp` bypasses intervening Return terminators, so:\n\n- N shadow frames between the throw site and the catch landing pad were permanently leaking on the per-thread `SHADOW_STACK`\n- Each subsequent throw grows the leak again\n- Long-running programs (and the test suite running ~128 tests sequentially) accumulate state monotonically\n\n\n1. Add `saved_shadow_depth: usize` to `ExceptionHandler` in `runtime/src/exception.rs`.\n2. Populate on `push_handler` from `crate::native_stack_trace::shadow_stack_depth()`.\n3. In `rayzor_throw_typed` (line 82-107), AFTER `capture_shadow_stack` (so the diagnostic trace stays full) but BEFORE `_longjmp`, call `crate::native_stack_trace::truncate_shadow_stack(handler.saved_shadow_depth)`.\n4. New `truncate_shadow_stack(depth)` API in `native_stack_trace.rs` that truncates `SHADOW_STACK.with(...)` down to `depth` entries.\n\n\n- The trapezoid pattern is structural: any future Try/Catch lowering with non-Return exits needs the same `saved_shadow_depth` discipline. Audit when adding async/coroutine throw paths.\n- Verifier suggested moving `truncate` BEFORE `capture_shadow_stack` \"so the current throw benefits too\" — declined because that would lose diagnostic frames between throw and saved depth. Current ordering preserves the trace for the catch handler's `e.details()` while still containing the leak.\n\n\nThe `bugs_test_exception_flake` SIGTRAP (~38% rate) is **not** caused by this leak — symptom is libmalloc `\"BUG IN CLIENT: memory corruption of free block\"` (UAF / double-free), not leak/OOM. Better-fitting next candidate per [[bugs-test-exception-flake]]: `Box\u003cHaxeString\u003e` ownership in `native_stack_trace::make_haxe_string:551-568`.\n\n\n- [[bugs-test-exception-flake]] — the user-visible SIGTRAP that triggered this investigation (still open)\n- [[bugs-cleanup-scopes-frees-captures]] / [[bugs-mark-escaping-incomplete]] — prior InsertFreePass class fixes; same \"compiler emits pop only at certain terminators\" structural shape\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_shadow_stack_leak_on_longjmp` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}